# Yard headroom

Never put a walkable ledge on rows 0–3. The scavenger is drawn 60px tall and a floor jump rises about 56px. A ledge on row 4 or lower leaves that room above him.

Walkable tiles: `=`, `+`, `>`, `<`, `E`, `M`, `K`.

`pack()` calls `ensureHeadroom()` and throws if a ledge is still too high. Do not disable that check. If a new yard cannot drop, add spare air rows in the middle — do not raise the top deck.

```
# BAD — jump leaves the canvas
.C............................C.   row 0
====....MMMMMM........MMMM======   row 1

# GOOD — first walkable row is 4+
................................   row 0
................................   row 1
................................   row 2
.C............................C.   row 3
====....MMMMMM........MMMM======   row 4
```

Moving plates use the same beam height as static walkways. They still must start on row 4 or below.
